    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay i have some pedialyte but he just spits it right back out every time i try to give him a full sip. i'm really scared he's just gonna get more weak. i saw online that some people use salt tablets or even just a bit of regular table salt in water to help with electrolytes when they're really dehydrated... would it be okay if i just gave him a tiny bit of that to see if it helps him stay hydrated better? i really wanna avoid the hospital if i can manage it here.",
